WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:15.000
As rector, it is a true honour and a great satisfaction for me

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.280
to preside over this launch event of the Andalusian Living Lab initiative.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.640
As you know, this is an initiative, a project led by the University of Jaén,

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:45.480
which aims to promote knowledge on a topic that has become a priority at European level and, of course, at national level too.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:52.980
Public bodies such as the Provincial Council of Jaén and the Regional Government of Andalusia take part in this Andalusian Living Lab,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:01:02.080
as well as research institutes and olive companies: in short, a consortium of organisations with wide experience in the olive sector,

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.140
led by the University of Jaén.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:10.920
Overall, the response has been very positive, exceeding any expectations we had beforehand.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.460
In general, the sector is keen to learn about the technological advances offered

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.880
by the University and by a very diverse, multidisciplinary consortium.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.080
Here today there are farmers, farming associations, cooperatives and olive mills

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.580
listening to how we are going to launch this Andalusian Living Lab,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:35.180
and how we will try to turn all the knowledge presented at this event

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.920
into products and business models they can apply in the field.
